1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,640
A hundred bucks a day beats a million. Unless you're old as hell.

2
00:00:04,360 --> 00:00:06,820
The choice is a million dollars cash, today.

3
00:00:07,300 --> 00:00:10,280
Or a hundred dollars every single day until you die.

4
00:00:10,700 --> 00:00:14,480
No taxes, no interest, no bullshit. Just two piles of money.

5
00:00:14,960 --> 00:00:17,640
And everyone's first instinct? Give me the damn million.

6
00:00:18,100 --> 00:00:20,140
Double-tap if you'd snatch it in half a second.

7
00:00:20,660 --> 00:00:23,700
But a hundred a day is about three thousand dollars a month.

8
00:00:24,060 --> 00:00:27,840
That's your rent, paid every month, forever, without lifting a finger.

9
00:00:27,840 --> 00:00:31,760
After one year, that's thirty-six thousand five hundred dollars.

10
00:00:32,320 --> 00:00:35,960
Then on day ten thousand, the daily money finally catches the million.

11
00:00:36,420 --> 00:00:39,960
That's about twenty-seven years. So now it's all about your age.

12
00:00:40,560 --> 00:00:43,320
Send this to the friend who'd spend the million on cars by Friday.

13
00:00:43,920 --> 00:00:47,300
Start at twenty-five and live to eighty, and you collect about two million.

14
00:00:47,680 --> 00:00:49,860
That's double, just for waking up every morning.

15
00:00:50,380 --> 00:00:52,020
Start at forty, and you still win.

16
00:00:52,780 --> 00:00:54,500
Follow, 'cause this is the part that stings.

17
00:00:54,900 --> 00:00:59,180
But start at sixty and make it to eighty? You get seven hundred thirty thousand.

18
00:00:59,660 --> 00:01:03,160
The boring million beats you by two hundred seventy thousand dollars.

19
00:01:03,680 --> 00:01:08,000
So the daily cash only wins after twenty-seven years. Brutal, right?

20
00:01:08,520 --> 00:01:10,660
Million or a hundred a day? One word.

